# Site-specific patterns for scripts/check-no-real-values.sh.
#
# Copy to `.private-patterns` (gitignored) and fill in the real values. This
# example file is tracked and must therefore stay free of them.
#
# One POSIX extended regex per line; `#` starts a comment. Matching is
# case-sensitive, so include both cases where it matters. Every staged file is
# checked against every pattern, and any match blocks the commit.
#
# Worth covering:
#
#   the internal domain, both cases        example\.lan|EXAMPLE\.LAN
#   the LDAP/DSM realm                     @LH-EXAMPLE\.LAN
#   real usernames / LDAP home dirs        \b(alice|bob)-[0-9]{7}\b
#   household and personal names           \b(Alice|Bob)\b
#   personal device names                  Pixel [0-9]+[a-z]?
#   the real WAN IP                        203\.0\.113\.[0-9]+
#
# Generic patterns (Synology volume paths, numeric PUID/PGID, non-example
# email addresses, private 10/172.16/192.168 host addresses, *.lan hostnames)
# are built into the script and need no entry here.
